# [[ .Name ]]

A [Quanarch](https://quanarch.org) quanar: it gives quans a place to live and
plugs in the quas they use. It holds no business logic.

```sh
npm run dev       # start the quanar
npm run build     # build for production
```

Every folder exports its contents through an `index.ts` barrel, and every
module is a folder named after it with an `index.ts(x)` inside.

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `src/core/plugs` | The quas this quanar plugs in, and how each one works. |
| `src/core/loader` | Where quans come from. `static-loader` reads `public/quans/`; swap it for any source. |
| `src/core/policy` | Which quans a user receives. |
| `src/core/shared` | Shares React with the quans it loads. |
| `src/pages`, `src/layouts`, `src/components`, `src/hooks` | The quanar's own interface. |
| `src/services`, `src/configs`, `src/constants`, `src/types`, `src/utils`, `src/assets` | Supporting code. |

Deliver a quan into this quanar from the quan's directory:

```sh
npm run build && npm run deliver -- ../[[ .Name ]]
```
